Camera device: characteristics, physical camera characteristics and capture results leave the
HAL with sensor orientation and lens pose re-expressed for the landscape natural orientation
(dogal-yon/hal/src/camera_natural_orientation.cpp). Request templates stay as the HAL made them:
apps send them back as request settings, and the HAL echoes request values (lens pose among
them) in its results, which are re-expressed once on the way out.

--- a/aidl/camera/device/convert.h
+++ b/aidl/camera/device/convert.h
@@ -48,6 +48,11 @@
 using ::aidl::android::hardware::camera::device::Stream;
 
 void convertToAidl(const camera_metadata_t* src, CameraMetadata* dest);
+// Googlebook OS (T870-araclar/dogal-yon/hal): metadata the framework interprets
+// (characteristics, capture results) with the values defined relative to the device's natural
+// orientation re-expressed for its landscape natural orientation. Request templates keep
+// convertToAidl: they come back as request settings and the HAL echoes them in its results.
+void convertToAidlNaturalOrientation(const camera_metadata_t* src, CameraMetadata* dest);
 
 bool convertFromAidl(const CameraMetadata& src, const camera_metadata_t** dst);
 
